      "text": "Adjust for the genotype G. G is a common cause of S and C, so it opens a backdoor path S <- G -> C that confounds the S->C effect; conditioning on G blocks it and satisfies the backdoor criterion. Do NOT adjust for tar T: T is a mediator on the causal path S -> T -> C. Conditioning on a mediator blocks part of the very effect you want to estimate (it would give only the direct S->C effect, biasing the total effect). So the valid adjustment set is {G}, not {G, T} and not {T}."
    }
  ],
  "role": "model"
}

